{
  "id": "0199897e6530-80d24237889186ca210d4b5e",
  "section": "Math",
  "domain": "Geometry and Trigonometry",
  "related_skills": [
    "Lines, angles, and triangles"
  ],
  "unit": "Unit 11 - Lines",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 11 - Lines for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<ul>\n<li><strong>Slope (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></math>):</strong> measures steepness.  </li>\n</ul>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>rise</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>run</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>y-intercept (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>):</strong> point where line crosses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>-axis.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>Equation form:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>\n\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br />\nFind slope and intercept of line through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<p>Equation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>. Plug <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\nFinal: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<h3>Slope-Intercept Form</h3>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></math>\n\n<h3>Point-Slope Form</h3>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>\n\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br />\nEquation of line through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> with slope <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p>Solve system of equations.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong><br />\nFind intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Set equal:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<p>Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\nIntersection = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.</p>\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Parallel lines:</strong> same slope, different intercepts.  </li>\n<li><strong>Perpendicular lines:</strong> slopes multiply to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> (negative reciprocals).  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br />\nFind equation of line parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Slope = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. Equation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 5</strong><br />\nFind equation of line perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>Slope = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\nEquation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Horizontal: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></math> (slope = 0).  </li>\n<li>Vertical: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></math> (slope undefined).  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 6</strong><br />\nEquation of line through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>:<br />\nAnswer: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 7</strong><br />\nEquation of line through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>:<br />\nAnswer: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Memorize slope formulas.  </li>\n<li>Parallel → same <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li>Perpendicular → <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>&#x000B7;</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li>Watch out for vertical/horizontal lines.  </li>\n<li>For intersections, substitution is often faster than graphing.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) Find slope and intercept of line through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.<br />\n2) Write equation of line with slope <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.<br />\n3) Find intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\n4) Write equation of line parallel to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math> through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.<br />\n5) Write equation of line perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>. Equation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2) Point-slope: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>3) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>. Intersection <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>4) Parallel slope <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>. Equation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>5) Perpendicular slope <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>. Equation: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">\n</code></pre>",
